# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure for the latest version of Qiskit Fermions"
msgstr "Pagpapangkat ng mga operator term: gamitin ang istruktura ng operator para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Qiskit Fermions"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure"
msgstr "Pagpapangkat ng mga operator term: gamitin ang istruktura ng operator"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"grouping-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"
msgstr "Pagpapangkat ng mga operator term: gamitin ang istruktura ng operator {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grouping is one of the operations under [`qiskit_fermions.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms\"), which collects routines that partition the terms of an operator based on their structure.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpapangkat ay isa sa mga operasyon sa ilalim ng [`qiskit_fermions.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms\"), na nagtitipon ng mga routine na nagpa-partition ng mga term ng operator batay sa istruktura ng mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As described in the [operators guide](operators#term-grouping), operators can store a **groups array**, an optional part of the sparse data structure that associates each term with a group index. Terms sharing the same group index form a group. This lets you use systematically use of the structure in downstream processing.\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng inilarawan sa [gabay sa mga operator](operators#term-grouping), maaaring mag-imbak ang mga operator ng **groups array**, isang opsyonal na bahagi ng sparse data structure na nag-uugnay ng bawat term sa isang group index. Ang mga term na may parehong group index ay bumubuo ng isang group. Pinapayagan ka nitong sistematikong magamit ang istruktura sa downstream na pagpoproseso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By grouping related terms (whether by physical properties, algebraic relationships, or problem-specific symmetries), you can unlock several benefits:\n"
msgstr "Sa pamamagitan ng pagpapangkat ng mga magkakaugnay na term (batay man sa pisikal na katangian, algebraic na ugnayan, o simetriyang partikular sa problema), makakakuha ka ng ilang benepisyo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimized circuit synthesis**: Grouped terms carry problem-specific information through the stack, enabling simpler optimization of the synthesized circuits. This results in reduced circuit depth and gate count.\n"
msgstr "**Optimized na circuit synthesis**: Dinadala ng mga pinangkat na term ang impormasyong partikular sa problema sa buong stack, kaya mas madali ang pag-optimize ng mga na-synthesize na circuit. Nagreresulta ito sa mas mababang circuit depth at bilang ng gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Physical structure preservation**: Groups encode meaningful structure from the original problem (for example, interaction patterns or symmetries) that can be used for more physically meaningful decompositions.\n"
msgstr "**Pagpepreserba ng pisikal na istruktura**: Ine-encode ng mga group ang makabuluhang istruktura mula sa orihinal na problema (halimbawa, mga pattern ng interaksyon o simetriya) na magagamit para sa mas makabuluhang pisikal na mga decomposition.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Flow set selection**: Grouping can naturally encode flow sets and other graph-theoretic structures relevant to quantum simulation, as shown in <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"
msgstr "**Pagpili ng flow set**: Natural na maisasa-code ng pagpapangkat ang mga flow set at iba pang graph-theoretic na istruktura na may kaugnayan sa quantum simulation, gaya ng ipinakita sa <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Improved algorithmic stability**: As demonstrated in the [SqDRIFT routine](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started), some algorithms can benefit from improved stability or performance due to the preservation of physical properties.\n"
msgstr "**Mas pinahusay na algorithmic stability**: Gaya ng ipinakita sa [SqDRIFT routine](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started), may ilang algorithm na makikinabang sa mas pinahusay na stability o performance dahil sa pagpepreserba ng mga pisikal na katangian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Product-formula factors**: A fermionic product formula splits an operator into its groups, so the grouping determines both the cost and the Trotter error of a time evolution. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"
msgstr "**Mga product-formula factor**: Hinahati ng fermionic product formula ang isang operator sa mga group nito, kaya ang pagpapangkat ang nagtatakda ng parehong gastos at ng Trotter error ng isang time evolution. Tingnan ang [Mag-synthesize ng Evolution gate sa fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage {#usage}"
msgstr "Paggamit {#usage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest way to define an operator grouping is by setting the target operator’s `groups` attribute. Below is an example for grouping terms according to the *line flow sets* as shown in Figure 1c of <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"
msgstr "Ang pinakasimpleng paraan para mag-define ng operator grouping ay ang pagtatakda ng `groups` attribute ng target na operator. Nasa ibaba ang halimbawa ng pagpapangkat ng mga term ayon sa *line flow sets* gaya ng ipinakita sa Figure 1c ng <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` module provides convenience methods for automatically identifying structure in an operator and assigning group indices accordingly.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Nagbibigay ang module na `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` ng mga convenience method para awtomatikong tukuyin ang istruktura sa isang operator at magtakda ng mga group index nang naaayon.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A simple directed graph on which to define a MajoranaOperator.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/grouping-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A simple directed graph on which to define a MajoranaOperator.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/grouping-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a simple two-by-three lattice of Majorana modes connected by directed edges. Each edge represents a term in the operator acting on the two connected modes. The goal is to group these terms according to their edge labels (shown on the graph). Terms connected by edges with the same label are placed in the same group. The following code shows how that can be done:\n"
msgstr "Ito ay isang simpleng two-by-three na lattice ng mga Majorana mode na konektado ng mga directed edge. Ang bawat edge ay kumakatawan sa isang term sa operator na kumikilos sa dalawang konektadong mode. Ang layunin ay pangkatin ang mga term na ito ayon sa mga label ng edge ng mga ito (ipinapakita sa graph). Ang mga term na konektado ng mga edge na may parehong label ay inilalagay sa iisang group. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na code kung paano ito magagawa:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import MajoranaOperator\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct operator directly using sparse arrays\n"
"    >>> # 7 terms, each with coefficient 1.0, modes from edge endpoints\n"
"    >>> op = MajoranaOperator(\n"
"    ...     coeffs=[1.0] * 7,\n"
"    ...     modes=[node for edge in edges for node in edge],\n"
"    ...     boundaries=[0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Assign group indices to terms (groups is part of the sparse data structure)\n"
"    >>> op.groups = groups\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Partition operator by groups\n"
"    >>> grouped_ops = op.split_out_groups()\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Inspect each group\n"
"    >>> for i, g in enumerate(grouped_ops):\n"
"    ...     print(f\"Group {i}: {list(sorted(g.iter_terms()))}\")\n"
"    Group 0: [([0, 1], (1+0j)), ([1, 2], (1+0j))]\n"
"    Group 1: [([3, 0], (1+0j)), ([5, 2], (1+0j))]\n"
"    Group 2: [([1, 4], (1+0j))]\n"
"    Group 3: [([4, 3], (1+0j)), ([5, 4], (1+0j))]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    #include <qiskit_fermions.h>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 7;\n"
"    uint64_t num_modes = 14;\n"
"    uint32_t modes[14] = {0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1, 4, 5, 2, 5, 4, 4, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[7] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0},\n"
"                             {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[8] = {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(num_terms, num_modes, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 7;\n"
"    uint64_t num_modes = 14;\n"
"    uint32_t modes[14] = {0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1, 4, 5, 2, 5, 4, 4, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[7] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0},\n"
"                             {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[8] = {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(num_terms, num_modes, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
