# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze a grouping {#analyze-a-grouping}"
msgstr "Pag-aralan ang isang grouping {#analyze-a-grouping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups prescribe no meaning of their own: the groups array records which terms belong together, never why. No routine in this library reports whether a grouping is “correct”, because there is no single notion of correctness to report against. Downstream consumers do, however, assume properties of a grouping, and the functions in this section let you check such an assumption up front rather than paying for it on every call.\n"
msgstr "Walang sariling kahulugan ang mga group: itinatala ng groups array kung aling mga term ang magkakasama, pero hindi kailanman kung bakit. Walang routine sa library na ito ang nag-uulat kung \"tama\" ang isang grouping, dahil walang iisang kahulugan ng kawastuhan na pagbabatayan. Gayunpaman, ang mga downstream na consumer ay may mga ipinapalagay na katangian ng isang grouping, at hinahayaan ka ng mga function sa seksyong ito na suriin ang ganoong palagay nang maaga sa halip na bayaran ito sa bawat tawag.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The most common convention is that each group is separately Hermitian. That is what makes fermionic randomized product formulas possible at all: a lone $a^\\dagger_p a_q$ with $p \\neq q$ is not Hermitian, so its time evolution is not unitary and it cannot be sampled on its own. Pairing it with $a^\\dagger_q a_p$ yields a group that can be.\n"
msgstr "Ang pinakakaraniwang convention ay ang bawat group ay hiwalay na Hermitian. Iyon ang nagpapagana sa fermionic randomized product formula sa unang lugar: ang nag-iisang $a^\\dagger_p a_q$ na may $p \\neq q$ ay hindi Hermitian, kaya hindi unitary ang time evolution nito at hindi ito mase-sample nang mag-isa. Kapag ipinares ito sa $a^\\dagger_q a_p$, nagkakaroon ng group na maaaring i-sample.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping import (\n"
"    ...     group_coeff_means,\n"
"    ...     groups_are_hermitian,\n"
"    ...     groups_have_uniform_coeffs,\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # a conjugate pair, plus one unpaired term. The operator is built from the sparse\n"
"    >>> # arrays rather than from a dictionary, because only the former fixes the term order\n"
"    >>> # that the group indices below are paired with.\n"
"    >>> pair_and_single = FermionOperator(\n"
"    ...     [1.0, 1.0, 1.0],\n"
"    ...     [True, False, True, False, True, False],\n"
"    ...     [0, 1, 1, 0, 2, 3],\n"
"    ...     [0, 2, 4, 6],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> pair_and_single.groups = [0, 0, 1]\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> groups_are_hermitian(pair_and_single)  # group 1 is unpaired\n"
"    [True, False]\n"
"    >>> group_coeff_means(pair_and_single)\n"
"    [1.0, 1.0]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 3;\n"
"    uint64_t num_actions = 6;\n"
"    bool actions[6] = {true, false, true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[6] = {0, 1, 1, 0, 2, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 2, 4, 6};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op =\n"
"        qf_ferm_op_new(num_terms, num_actions, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 3;\n"
"    uint64_t num_actions = 6;\n"
"    bool actions[6] = {true, false, true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[6] = {0, 1, 1, 0, 2, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 2, 4, 6};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op =\n"
"        qf_ferm_op_new(num_terms, num_actions, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_set_groups(op, groups, num_terms);\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_set_groups(op, groups, num_terms);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    bool hermitian[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_groups_are_hermitian(op, 1e-8, hermitian);\n"
msgstr ""
"    bool hermitian[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_groups_are_hermitian(op, 1e-8, hermitian);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    double means[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_group_coeff_means(op, means);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    double means[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_group_coeff_means(op, means);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "One group index per term is enforced {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"
msgstr "Isang group index bawat term ang ipinapatupad {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The groups array holds one index per term, and assigning one of a different length raises. Nothing downstream re-checks the invariant, so it is enforced where the indices enter the operator: an array that is too short would silently drop trailing terms, and one that is too long would invent groups that no term carries.\n"
msgstr "Ang groups array ay may hawak na isang index bawat term, at ang pagtatakda ng array na magkaiba ang haba ay nagtataas ng error. Walang downstream na muling sumusuri sa invariant na ito, kaya ipinapatupad ito sa mismong pagpasok ng mga index sa operator: ang masyadong maikling array ay tahimik na mag-aalis ng mga huling term, at ang masyadong mahaba ay lilikha ng mga group na walang term na nagdadala.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearing the group indices by assigning `None` is always allowed.\n"
msgstr "Palaging pinapayagan ang pag-clear ng mga group index sa pamamagitan ng pagtatakda ng `None`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two checks are independent {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"
msgstr "Magkahiwalay ang dalawang pagsusuri {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") reports whether a group’s coefficients agree, which is the assumption [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") makes when it averages magnitudes. It is not a weaker form of the Hermiticity check: neither check implies the other, in either direction.\n"
msgstr "Iniuulat ng [`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") kung nagkakasundo ang mga coefficient ng isang group, na siyang ipinapalagay ng [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") kapag nag-a-average ito ng mga magnitude. Hindi ito mas mahinang bersyon ng pagsusuri sa Hermiticity: walang pagsusuring nagpapahiwatig ng isa pa, sa alinmang direksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian conjugate pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form.\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, ikinukumpara ang mga magnitude, dahil iyon ang a-average-in ng [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\"). Ang Hermitian conjugate pair na may mga complex na coefficient ay may magkapantay na magnitude pero hindi magkapantay na coefficient, kaya natutugunan lamang nito ang default na anyo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") inherits the one-sided guarantee of [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): a `True` entry is always reliable, while a `False` entry is reliable only for operator types whose normal form is a genuine canonical form. Consult the specific operator type to find out which applies.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Namamana ng [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") ang isang-panig na garantiya ng [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): laging maaasahan ang entry na `True`, habang ang entry na `False` ay maaasahan lamang para sa mga operator type na ang normal form ay tunay na canonical form. Sumangguni sa partikular na operator type para malaman kung alin ang naaangkop.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

